        "input": {
          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "After the motor responds, the sensor measures again and the loop repeats. Larger gains are not automatically better: poor tuning can create overshoot, noise sensitivity, or oscillation. Engineers start with performance requirements, tune deliberately, and keep the controller as simple as the application allows. A PI controller may be enough when derivative action adds little value."
