        "input": {
          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "The proportional term reacts to the error right now. The integral term accumulates error over time, helping remove a persistent offset. The derivative term responds to how quickly error is changing, which can anticipate motion and reduce overshoot. Their weighted sum becomes the control input sent to the system."
        },
